:"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Solve $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} - 2\\dfrac{dy}{dx} + 5y = e^{2x}\\sin x$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1444,1405,108]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Use method of variation of parameters to solve\n\n$$\ny'' - 6y' + 9y = \\frac{e^{3x}}{x^2}\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1544,1405,144]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Find all the eigenvalues and any two of the eigenvectors of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&1&3\\\\1&5&1\\\\3&1&1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1680,1405,200]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Use Newton's divided difference formula to find the interpolating polynomial for the following data and hence find $y$ when $x=8$.\n\n| $x$ | 0 | 1 | 2 | 5 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| $y$ | 2 | 3 | 12 | 147 |","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-8-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,94,1405,262],"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-8-diagram-1","caption":"Data table for Newton's divided difference formula. (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-8-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,94,1405,262]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-9","number":"3C","markdown":"Use Simpson’s $\\tfrac{3}{8}$ rule to find an approximate value of $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\sqrt{\\cos\\theta}\\,d\\theta$ by taking six equal subintervals, correct to four decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-9-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,348,1405,128]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-10","number":"4A","markdown":"Use Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to construct the orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ from the set of vectors $\\{(1,2,2),(-1,0,2),(0,0,1)\\}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-10-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,468,1405,144]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Use Taylor’s series method to find an approximate value of $y$ at $x=0.1$ given $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=-xy^2$, $y(0)=1$, up to 5th order terms.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-11-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,604,1405,100]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Use Regula Falsi method to find the real root of the equation\n\n$$\nxe^x - \\cos x = 0,\n$$\n\nlying between 0.4 and 0.6. Carry out 4 iterations, correct to four decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,696,1405,202]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Test whether $B=\\{(3,0,2),(7,0,9),(4,1,2)\\}$ forms a basis for $\\mathbb{R}^3$. If so, express $(1,2,3)$ in terms of basis vectors.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,890,1405,93]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Solve the system of equations by Gauss elimination method\n\n$$\n6x_1 - 8x_2 + 10x_3 = -2\n$$\n\n$$\n-6x_1 + 4x_2 + 2x_3 = 2\n$$\n\n$$\n12x_1 + 16x_2 - 2x_3 = 70\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-14-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,975,1405,253]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"4bc93dc1e9246869294d-q-15","number":"5C","markdown":"Use Gauss Seidel method to solve the following system of equations by taking $x^{(0)}=y^{(0)}=z^{(0)}=1$ and carry out four iterations and correct to four decimal places.\n\n$$\nx+y+54z=110\n$$\n\n$$\n27x+6y-z=54\n$$\n\n$$\n6x+15y+2z=72\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/4bc93dc1e9246869294d/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,1220,1405,660]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4-mini. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
